Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:37:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] [Test][Qwen4Exp] Keep the pipeline-parallel contracts
 under regression guards

#60234 absorbed the code of this series' first three patches;
their regression tests had no upstream equivalent: the MTP drafter
drafts on the last rank, PP is accepted with and without PLE, the PP
wire carries hidden states only (ids ride the stage-local #61016
flow), and non-first ranks feed runner input ids to the decoder
layers. The bare-instance construction now binds upstream's
factory-made make_empty_intermediate_tensors where the model class
does not define one, so the wire-shape assertion holds on both the
plain and the int8-hop build.
